# the grove reach's caller identity
#
# 🔴 THIS REPO IS PUBLIC AND THE COLLABORATOR'S IS PRIVATE. their account id and
#    role name live in a private tree, so a constant in our source would publish
#    another org's identity to the world — their disclosure to make, not ours.
#
# .note = these are NOT secrets. both values land in the applied trust policy and
#         are readable by anyone with `iam:GetRole` on demo. this is disclosure
#         control, never secrecy: it keeps a foreign org's identity out of a
#         public git history, and buys naught beyond that.
#
# .note = the vars are named for the REACH, never for the collaborator, so the
#         collaborator's name stays absent from source too.
#
# to use:
#   cp -n provision/aws.auth/account=demo/.env.example provision/aws.auth/account=demo/.env
#   # fill in the values from the collaborator's private tree, then:
#   source provision/aws.auth/account=demo/.env
#
# ⚠️ a wrong value here is a PERMANENTLY DEAD REACH that both halves apply
#    cleanly into. the plan read is what catches it — the resolved principal arn
#    shows in the plan diff, so read it before every apply.

# the collaborator's aws account id — 12 digits
# e.g., GROVE_REACH_CAMP_ACCOUNT_ID=000000000000
export GROVE_REACH_CAMP_ACCOUNT_ID=__the_camp_account_id__

# the collaborator's grove role name — the role our trust policy names as principal
# e.g., GROVE_REACH_CAMP_ROLE_NAME=example-camp-grove-role
export GROVE_REACH_CAMP_ROLE_NAME=__the_camp_grove_role_name__

# the demo role a grove assumes — OUR arn, and only the live-reach check reads it
#
# .why = it carries two loads. it OPTS IN `resources.reach.integration.test.ts`,
#        which can run only from a grove box, and it supplies the arn — so our
#        demo account id stays out of a public git history too. resolve it with
#        `aws sts get-caller-identity` under live demo creds.
#
# .note = unset is the NORMAL state. cicd and every non-grove box leave it
#         absent, and that live-reach check then declines rather than fails.
#
# e.g., GROVE_REACH_TARGET_ROLE_ARN=arn:aws:iam::000000000000:role/ehmpathy-demo-for-grove
# export GROVE_REACH_TARGET_ROLE_ARN=__the_demo_reach_role_arn__
